  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{1}{C}=\\frac{1}{C_{1}}+\\frac{1}{C_{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{2}{4}$\r\n$C=2 \\mu F$\r\n$2 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$ will be parallel to $4 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$. so the resultant capacitance\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2016_phy_a1.png\">\r\n\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\frac{1}{C^{\\prime \\prime}} &=\\frac{1}{4 \\mu F}+\\frac{1}{4 \\mu F}=\\frac{2}{4} \\mu F \\\\ C^{-} &=2 \\mu F \\\\ C_{A Q} &=2 \\mu F+6 \\mu F \\\\ &=8 \\mu F \\end{aligned}$",
